certain urban libraries, watch TVs in bars, use public wifi for laptops and smartphones.<br /> <br /> You can drive fast cars, run like an animal, philosophize, write the next Great American Novel, or spend a few hours in all night movie theaters. With the willingness necessary to scrounge up resources, you can do just about anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T06:04:32-07:00","id":1386374,"title":"","content":"trolling lupines","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T07:59:53-07:00","id":1386404,"title":"","content":"Chase him through the woods, staying just out of sight, while screaming and throwing rabbits and squirrels at him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T10:56:16-07:00","id":1386433,"title":"","content":"Is the hitchhiker a serial killer? If so, take some time to enjoy the surprised expression on his face","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T11:56:20-07:00","id":1386447,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10998_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10998\" data-vbnamecard=\"10998\">Pleiades</a> nice! \ud83d\ude02","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T14:34:53-07:00","id":1386497,"title":"","content":"A lot depends on just how late it is, and what the weather is like.<br /> <br /> Best-case scenario, it is an hour or two after sunset in the winter in a mild climate. So, say around 8pm or so in rural Florida? (I used to live <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/@27.2378247,-80.8298468,3a,86.2y,348.07h,94t/data=!3m6!1e1!3m4!1srapYHO0F_K2YffhKOoSoaA!2e0!7i13312!8i6656\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.)<ul><li>Most towns have a movie theater. Keep it light, though. No subtitles. Nobody wants to be alone at night after watching Czech nuwave arthouse cinema.</li> <li>Hit a <a href=\"https://www.thrillist.com/drink/nation/last-call-in-every-state-in-america\" target=\"_blank\">local bar</a>. Play some pool. Watch some tv. There might even be music/dancing, or a big game on.</li> <li>Most retail is open until 9 or 10. Drug stores, groceries, bookstores, diners, thrift shops, etc. Not the opera, but passes the time.</li> <li>Fast food... especially the parking lots... can be a real social scene. Convenience stores, too.</li> <li>Church events might be good. Concerts, speakers, evening services, etc. It's sociable, if you can pass for a normal. Be careful of True Faith.</li> <li>If bat form is an option, sneak into a house, and watch the family. Or, just hang and watch whatever they're watching on tv.</li> <li>Again bat form (or if you're just good at being ignored), and hang out at a medical center or police station. Lots of workplace dramas to watch.</li> <li>Find a house... or a clearing in the woods... with a party and crash it.</li> <li>Find water and go swimming. You're beyond mosquitos and drowning, so, yay.</li> <li>High school sports! OMG, in some places a well-timed football game can be a Very Big Deal.</li> <li>Go bowling. Seriously, on a quiet night you can milk the lane for hours.</li> <li>Show up at a chain restaurant in uniform and begin working. If it's busy, it's possible they'll be so relieved no one will ask questions. Don't forget to split your tips with the kitchen.</li> <li>Wander through backyards until you find a dog you can chat with.</li> <li>If you get really lonely hit some 12-step meetings. They welcome pale strangers, and won't be offended if you refuse the donuts.</li> </ul><br /> Mediocre-case scenario, it is late at night, like after 10 or 11 pm. Again, a mild climate helps.<ul><li>Movies might have a late-show on the weekend. Pick something deep and meaningful. Try to get somebody to discuss it with you at length in the parking lot.</li> <li>RHPS!</li> <li>Bars become more boisterous on a weekend, more depressing on a weeknight.</li> <li>Walmart is usually 24 hours. Everyone looks like a vampire at 3am under fluorescent lights, so you're probably safe.</li> <li>Break into a store and browse. Nightvision makes a bookstore your personal library.</li> <li>Find a sex-worker and hire them for talking. This is weirdly common. Possibly, the saddest thing ever, but common.</li> <li>Cruise alleys looking for a kid sneaking out of the house. Follow them. No one sneaks out to do something boring.</li> <li>Get a cheap (or, expensive, I don't mean to be &quot;clannist&quot;) motel room. Hot shower. Cable tv. Internet. Not a bad way to spend a few hours.</li> <li>Cow tipping. (Ask first, just to be polite.)</li> <li>Diners are often 24 hours. If you tip well, the server won't care if you don't actually eat. A twenty for an untouched cup of coffee, and a few hours of chit-chat sounds about right. Avoid busy times, or at least tip much better.</li> <li>Walk. Run. Walk. Run. Repeat.</li> <li>Plan how you will become the Prince of Miami and pass all sorts of crazy rules. &quot;No hunting except on salt water boats!&quot;</li> <li>Sit on a park bench and read. You have night vision; use it.</li> <li>Speaking of night vision... know what daysiders can't do? See sweeping mountain vistas and charming landscapes at night. You can. Go on a <a href=\"https://newenglandwithlove.com/new-england-fall-foliage-tours/\" target=\"_blank\">leaf-peeping tour of New England</a> at Midnight. So much less traffic at 1 am!</li> <li>Find a stray dog and, using Animalism, teach them <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RTTfmoklBok\" target=\"_blank\">truly amazing tricks</a>. Like how to dance the tango, or sing a Liza Minelli song. Drop it off at the animal shelter to be instantly adopted. (Now, can I spend xp on Humanity?)</li> </ul><br /> Worst-case scenario. It's 3am. In western Nebraska. In a snowstorm.<ul><li>Hitchhike. People are much more likely to pick you up in a snowstorm. Tell them your life story. Your elaborately fictional life-story.</li> <li>Play Santa. Break into the Dollar Store and steal a trashbag full of toys. Deliver them to random porches.</li> <li>Turn on Obfuscate and &quot;water-ski&quot; off the back of a snowplow.</li> <li>Steal a ski-doo! <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HoZBi04afwc\" target=\"_blank\">Run it on streets</a>!</li> <li>Turn into a wolf and mount a dog doing its business in a backyard. When the owner looks outside and freaks, stare at the human, smile, and keep going.</li> <li>Find somebody walking five miles to their low-wage job. They're obviously a survivor type. Embrace them. Spend five minutes explaining things, then walk away.</li> <li>Steal a car and get into a minor fender-bender. Dealing with the other driver and police should take an hour or two. Is there no end to your boredom?</li> <li>Shovel the snow from all the driveways in the neighborhood. If anyone confronts you, tell them you're staying with &quot;the Millers down the street&quot;. There are always Millers down the street.</li> <li>Walk into a hospital emergency room and tell them you're not feeling well. Let them examine you. Do not use blush of life. Zany hijinx surely ensue.</li> <li>Stand in the main intersection and scream, &quot;I am the uncontested vampire Prince of this metropolis! None may defy me!&quot; Bonus points if there is no traffic light.</li> <li>Build seven snowmen in the town park. One for each clan.</li> <li>For God's sake, just get a hotel room like a normal person. It's warm, quiet, and comfortable. Read a book. Watch a little tv. Maybe wander wikipedia.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"dat